      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In view of current interest in the so-called \"risk factors\" of atherosclerotic cardiovascular diseases and the usefulness of preventive dietary measures, a review is given of the published data from long-term prospective studies. Opinions concerning the importance of the various lipoprotein classes as risk factors and reports of a decrease in the concentration of the allegedly \"protective\" high-density lipoproteins by consumption of polyunsaturated fatty acids are discussed. An up-to-date summary of current scientific developments relative to this problem is presented."},
